{"h":"<style>\n.vbm [hidden]{display:none!important}\n.vbm .vbm-dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(250px,1fr));gap:10px;margin:14px 0 0;max-width:980px}\n.vbm .vbm-d{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;background:var(--surface);padding:12px 16px 14px}\n.vbm .vbm-d h3{font:700 12px var(--sans);letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);margin:0}\n.vbm .vbm-d .when{display:block;font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:27px;line-height:1.1;margin:6px 0 4px}\n.vbm .vbm-d p{margin:6px 0 0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.5}\n.vbm .vbm-tag{display:inline-block;font:700 11.5px var(--sans);letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;border:1.5px solid var(--gold);color:var(--ink);border-radius:999px;padding:1px 9px;margin-left:8px;vertical-align:5px}\n.vbm .vbm-past{border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:5px solid var(--gold);background:var(--surface);border-radius:0 12px 12px 0;padding:10px 14px;margin:12px 0 0;max-width:80ch;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5}\n.vbm .vbm-go{margin:14px 0 0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 10px;align-items:center}\n.vbm .vbm-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;padding:8px 16px;border-radius:999px;background:var(--accent);border:1px solid var(--accent);color:var(--surface);font:600 14.5px var(--sans);text-decoration:none;max-width:100%}\n.vbm .vbm-btn:focus-visible,.vbm a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ink);outline-offset:2px}\n.vbm h3.vh{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:23px;line-height:1.15;margin:22px 0 4px}\n.vbm h4{font:600 15.5px var(--sans);margin:12px 0 2px}\n.vbm .vt{max-width:80ch;line-height:1.55;margin:6px 0 0;font-size:15px}\n.vbm ul.vbm-l{margin:6px 0 0;padding-left:20px;max-width:80ch}.vbm ul.vbm-l li{margin:7px 0;line-height:1.5;font-size:15px}\n.vbm a.vbm-s{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap}\n.vbm .vbm-ck{color:var(--muted);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.5;margin:14px 0 0;max-width:80ch}\n.vbm ol.vbm-src{font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;padding-left:22px;margin:8px 0 12px}.vbm ol.vbm-src li{margin:5px 0}\n.vbm .vbm-src small{color:var(--muted)}\n.vbm .lvmore{margin:12px 0 0}\n</style><section class=\"bsec vbm\" id=\"mail\" aria-labelledby=\"mail-h\"><h2 id=\"mail-h\" data-t=\"1unlq8t\">Vote by mail or absentee</h2><p class=\"sub\" data-t=\"1k60vhs\">Can&rsquo;t get to your polling place on Election Day? Here is how to vote by mail in <span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span>, from the state&rsquo;s own election office and its laws. Checked <time datetime=\"2026-10-21\" data-tf=\"{&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;,&quot;year&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">October 21, 2026</time>.</p><div class=\"vbm-dl\"><div class=\"vbm-d\"><h3 data-t=\"1kaxy8n\">Ask for your ballot by</h3><b class=\"when\" data-t=\"135q7nt\"><time datetime=\"2026-10-29\" data-tf=\"{&quot;weekday&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">Thursday, October 29</time><span class=\"vbm-tag\" data-vbm-past=\"2026-10-29\">Passed</span></b><p><span lang=\"en\">Applications must be in by Thursday, October 29, 2026 (the rule: no less than 5 days before the election; the State Board&#x27;s Voting by Mail page says requests by mail must be RECEIVED by your election authority by that date). An application delivered in person may be made up to Monday, November 2, 2026 (no less than 1 day before). The State Board urges applying as early as possible.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmj2awazxG5oLYFkE33dlxTqFgJUGePoYJvFoQzCF0NPPhk%2bkCUeTnMY7WNUFQszxqTDQ9jXur%2fsETCB7SX822PFAg5OWTXYGBk9j5PCx45ROsQc0E6Cb0pA%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Voting by Mail: Who May Apply for a Vote By Mail Ballot? (10 ILCS 5/19, 5/20), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></p></div><div class=\"vbm-d\"><h3 data-t=\"0q8rlso\">Send it back by</h3><b class=\"when\" data-t=\"135q7nt\"><time datetime=\"2026-11-03\" data-tf=\"{&quot;weekday&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">Tuesday, November 3</time><span class=\"vbm-tag\" data-vbm-past=\"2026-11-03\" hidden>Passed</span></b><p><span lang=\"en\">By mail: postmarked on or before Election Day, Tuesday, November 3, 2026, and received by your election authority by Tuesday, November 17, 2026 (within 14 days). In a drop box: by the close of polls, 7 p.m. on November 3, 2026.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmJ%2bGs6YFATVXPZF6r1FbitENUkm%2fywKrEQArnBU6aOPGahVJq1yE9PG9ksIX8KZJgTJ0G5ME8mTXm2phBu7K0HRGxGCxNtZaL%2b1iPXZ9SlCSPTm68r48uJcHoU8RSIsyrXM3nKvqxLmJAufgl412N%2fQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"2026 Vote-By-Mail Frequently Asked Questions (rev. 8/2026), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></p></div></div><p class=\"vbm-past\" data-vbm-past=\"2026-10-29\"><b data-t=\"0h10l0e\">The last day to ask for a ballot by mail has passed.</b> <span data-vbm-until=\"2026-11-02\" data-t=\"0hq6bu3\">You can still vote in person, early or on Election Day, <time datetime=\"2026-11-03\" data-tf=\"{&quot;weekday&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">Tuesday, November 3</time>.</span><span data-vbm-past=\"2026-11-02\" hidden data-t=\"1qmjo5n\">You can still vote in person on Election Day, <time datetime=\"2026-11-03\" data-tf=\"{&quot;weekday&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">Tuesday, November 3</time>.</span> <span data-vbm-until=\"2026-11-02\" data-t=\"1258jaf\">Early voting in person runs through <time datetime=\"2026-11-02\" data-tf=\"{&quot;weekday&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;,&quot;year&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">Monday, November 2, 2026</time>.</span> <span data-t=\"1ds6ate\"><a href=\"#mail-early\">When and where to vote early</a>.</span></p><p class=\"vbm-go\"><a class=\"vbm-btn\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/ElectionOperations/VotingByMailAgreement.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span data-t=\"11wqgc2\">Ask for a ballot online, on <span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span>&rsquo;s own site</span></a></p><p class=\"vt\" data-lv-max=\"2\" data-t=\"0npboy3\">At school away from home, in <span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span> or in another state? What <span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span> says about students is under Show more.</p><div class=\"lvmore\" data-lv-max=\"2\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tca-lv-more\" data-lv-more=\"3\" data-t=\"0l1c6cp\">Show more: students, how to ask and send it back, what the envelope needs, tracking, early voting, military and overseas</button></div><div data-lv=\"3\"><h3 class=\"vh\" data-t=\"0itlfhn\">Who can vote by mail</h3><p class=\"vt\"><span lang=\"en\">No reason is needed. Any registered voter can vote by mail in Illinois. Illinois no longer uses the word &#x27;absentee&#x27;; a vote-by-mail ballot is the same thing.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmJ%2bGs6YFATVXPZF6r1FbitENUkm%2fywKrEQArnBU6aOPGahVJq1yE9PG9ksIX8KZJgTJ0G5ME8mTXm2phBu7K0HRGxGCxNtZaL%2b1iPXZ9SlCSPTm68r48uJcHoU8RSIsyrXM3nKvqxLmJAufgl412N%2fQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"2026 Vote-By-Mail Frequently Asked Questions (rev. 8/2026), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></p><h3 class=\"vh\" data-t=\"1s8mt3z\">How to ask for a ballot</h3><ul class=\"vbm-l\"><li><b data-t=\"1naru8c\">Online.</b> <span lang=\"en\">The State Board of Elections&#x27; site sends you to your local election authority (your county clerk or city/county election commission): either its online application or a printable form with instructions. Send the application to that local office, not to the State Board.</span> <a href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/ElectionOperations/VotingByMailAgreement.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-t=\"03wbwnq\">Open it</a> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmJ%2bGs6YFATVXPZF6r1FbitENUkm%2fywKrEQArnBU6aOPGahVJq1yE9PG9ksIX8KZJgTJ0G5ME8mTXm2phBu7K0HRGxGCxNtZaL%2b1iPXZ9SlCSPTm68r48uJcHoU8RSIsyrXM3nKvqxLmJAufgl412N%2fQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"2026 Vote-By-Mail Frequently Asked Questions (rev. 8/2026), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></li><li><b data-t=\"1o1umaf\">By mail.</b> <span lang=\"en\">Mail the application to your local election authority. A signature is required on a paper application; one made online does not need one.</span> <a href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/ElectionOperations/ElectionAuthorities.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-t=\"03wbwnq\">Open it</a> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmj2awazxG5oLYFkE33dlxTqFgJUGePoYJvFoQzCF0NPPhk%2bkCUeTnMY7WNUFQszxqTDQ9jXur%2fsETCB7SX822PFAg5OWTXYGBk9j5PCx45ROsQc0E6Cb0pA%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Voting by Mail: Who May Apply for a Vote By Mail Ballot? (10 ILCS 5/19, 5/20), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></li><li><b data-t=\"0ffqycr\">In person.</b> <span lang=\"en\">Apply at your local election authority&#x27;s office.</span> <a href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/ElectionOperations/ElectionAuthorities.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-t=\"03wbwnq\">Open it</a> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmj2awazxG5oLYFkE33dlxTqFgJUGePoYJvFoQzCF0NPPhk%2bkCUeTnMY7WNUFQszxqTDQ9jXur%2fsETCB7SX822PFAg5OWTXYGBk9j5PCx45ROsQc0E6Cb0pA%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Voting by Mail: Who May Apply for a Vote By Mail Ballot? (10 ILCS 5/19, 5/20), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></li></ul><h3 class=\"vh\" data-t=\"1mswm78\">How to send it back</h3><ul class=\"vbm-l\"><li><b data-t=\"1o1umaf\">By mail.</b> <span lang=\"en\">Some election authorities pay the return postage and some do not; your ballot&#x27;s instructions say which. The Postal Service delivers every ballot even if postage is short, and election offices must accept it.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmJ%2bGs6YFATVXPZF6r1FbitENUkm%2fywKrEQArnBU6aOPGahVJq1yE9PG9ksIX8KZJgTJ0G5ME8mTXm2phBu7K0HRGxGCxNtZaL%2b1iPXZ9SlCSPTm68r48uJcHoU8RSIsyrXM3nKvqxLmJAufgl412N%2fQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"2026 Vote-By-Mail Frequently Asked Questions (rev. 8/2026), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></li><li><b data-t=\"1edq8t5\">Drop box.</b> <span lang=\"en\">About half of Illinois&#x27;s election authorities offer secure drop boxes, open until 7 p.m. on Election Day. The State Board lists them.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmJ%2bGs6YFATVXPZF6r1FbitENUkm%2fywKrEQArnBU6aOPGahVJq1yE9PG9ksIX8KZJgTJ0G5ME8mTXm2phBu7K0HRGxGCxNtZaL%2b1iPXZ9SlCSPTm68r48uJcHoU8RSIsyrXM3nKvqxLmJAufgl412N%2fQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"2026 Vote-By-Mail Frequently Asked Questions (rev. 8/2026), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></li><li><b data-t=\"0ffqycr\">In person.</b> <span lang=\"en\">Deliver it to your election authority&#x27;s office. Completed mail ballots are NOT accepted at polling places or early voting sites; there you will be offered the choice of giving up the mail ballot and voting in person instead.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmJ%2bGs6YFATVXPZF6r1FbitENUkm%2fywKrEQArnBU6aOPGahVJq1yE9PG9ksIX8KZJgTJ0G5ME8mTXm2phBu7K0HRGxGCxNtZaL%2b1iPXZ9SlCSPTm68r48uJcHoU8RSIsyrXM3nKvqxLmJAufgl412N%2fQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"2026 Vote-By-Mail Frequently Asked Questions (rev. 8/2026), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></li><li><b data-t=\"0h5pnnm\">Someone else for you.</b> <span lang=\"en\">Anyone you choose may deliver your ballot, if you and that person fill out the statement on the ballot envelope about who is delivering it.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmJ%2bGs6YFATVXPZF6r1FbitENUkm%2fywKrEQArnBU6aOPGahVJq1yE9PG9ksIX8KZJgTJ0G5ME8mTXm2phBu7K0HRGxGCxNtZaL%2b1iPXZ9SlCSPTm68r48uJcHoU8RSIsyrXM3nKvqxLmJAufgl412N%2fQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"2026 Vote-By-Mail Frequently Asked Questions (rev. 8/2026), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></li></ul><h3 class=\"vh\" data-t=\"0ohes51\">What the envelope needs</h3><p class=\"vt\"><span lang=\"en\">Sign the statement (affidavit) on the ballot envelope; it says you voted your own ballot in secret. If someone helps you mark your ballot, their name and address go on the envelope. A candidate may not help you unless they are your spouse, parent, child or sibling.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmj2awazxG5oLYFkE33dlxTqFgJUGePoYJvFoQzCF0NPPhk%2bkCUeTnMY7WNUFQszxqTDQ9jXur%2fsETCB7SX822PFAg5OWTXYGBk9j5PCx45ROsQc0E6Cb0pA%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Voting by Mail: Who May Apply for a Vote By Mail Ballot? (10 ILCS 5/19, 5/20), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></p><h3 class=\"vh\" data-t=\"17qn5hj\">Track your ballot</h3><p class=\"vt\"><a href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/ElectionOperations/ElectionAuthorities.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-t=\"1qpsit4\">Track your ballot on <span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span>&rsquo;s own site</a> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmJ%2bGs6YFATVXPZF6r1FbitENUkm%2fywKrEQArnBU6aOPGahVJq1yE9PG9ksIX8KZJgTJ0G5ME8mTXm2phBu7K0HRGxGCxNtZaL%2b1iPXZ9SlCSPTm68r48uJcHoU8RSIsyrXM3nKvqxLmJAufgl412N%2fQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"2026 Vote-By-Mail Frequently Asked Questions (rev. 8/2026), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></p><h3 class=\"vh\" id=\"mail-early\" data-t=\"1yat064\">Vote early in person instead</h3><p class=\"vt\"><span lang=\"en\">Early voting in person is available through Monday, November 2, 2026; your election authority sets the places and hours.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/ElectionOperations/VotingByMail.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Voting by Mail: Next Election, 2026 General Election, Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></p><h3 class=\"vh\" data-t=\"1c23ah5\">Students</h3><h4 data-t=\"0qh9s6l\">At school in <span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span>, away from home</h4><p class=\"vt\"><span lang=\"en\">The state&#x27;s pages do not speak to students separately. Its general rule: any properly registered Illinois voter may vote by mail, and applications go to the local election authority where you are registered.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmj2awazxG5oLYFkE33dlxTqFgJUGePoYJvFoQzCF0NPPhk%2bkCUeTnMY7WNUFQszxqTDQ9jXur%2fsETCB7SX822PFAg5OWTXYGBk9j5PCx45ROsQc0E6Cb0pA%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Voting by Mail: Who May Apply for a Vote By Mail Ballot? (10 ILCS 5/19, 5/20), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></p><h4 data-t=\"001gk3p\">At school in another state, with <span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span> as home</h4><p class=\"vt\"><span lang=\"en\">The state&#x27;s pages do not speak separately to students in another state. Its general rule: any properly registered Illinois voter may vote by mail, with the deadlines above. A U.S. citizen temporarily out of the country who keeps a precinct residence in Illinois may also vote by mail.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmj2awazxG5oLYFkE33dlxTqFgJUGePoYJvFoQzCF0NPPhk%2bkCUeTnMY7WNUFQszxqTDQ9jXur%2fsETCB7SX822PFAg5OWTXYGBk9j5PCx45ROsQc0E6Cb0pA%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Voting by Mail: Who May Apply for a Vote By Mail Ballot? (10 ILCS 5/19, 5/20), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></p><h3 class=\"vh\" data-t=\"074u44j\">Military and overseas</h3><p class=\"vt\"><span lang=\"en\">Military voters and their families, and citizens living outside the U.S., can register and request a ballot through Illinois&#x27;s MOVE site and download the ballot. A request mailed from outside the U.S. that arrives at least 30 days before the election gets a full ballot; one arriving later gets a federal-offices-only ballot. Ballots for these voters go out 45 days before the election. A federal write-in ballot is a backup if yours may not arrive in time.</span> <a class=\"vbm-s\" href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmj2awazxG5oLYFkE33dlxTqFgJUGePoYJvFoQzCF0NPPhk%2bkCUeTnMY7WNUFQszxqTDQ9jXur%2fsETCB7SX822PFAg5OWTXYGBk9j5PCx45ROsQc0E6Cb0pA%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Voting by Mail: Who May Apply for a Vote By Mail Ballot? (10 ILCS 5/19, 5/20), Illinois State Board of Elections\" data-t=\"1nzewho\">(official page)</a></p><p class=\"vt\"><a href=\"https://www.fvap.gov/illinois\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-t=\"181taje\"><span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span> in the <span translate=\"no\">Federal Voting Assistance Program</span>&rsquo;s guide</a></p><h3 class=\"vh\" data-t=\"1397uds\">Good to know</h3><ul class=\"vbm-l\"><li lang=\"en\">Illinois counts a mailed ballot that is postmarked by Election Day and arrives within 14 days, so unofficial results can change for two weeks after Election Day.</li><li lang=\"en\">To check on your ballot, the State Board&#x27;s FAQ says to contact your election authority; many have status tools on their own websites. The track link goes to the State Board&#x27;s list of the 108 local election authorities.</li><li lang=\"en\">If your mail ballot is rejected, your election authority must tell you within two days and give you a chance to fix the problem (State Board FAQ).</li><li lang=\"en\">Mail is not always postmarked the day you send it; the State Board suggests asking for a hand postmark at the post office counter when mailing close to Election Day (its &#x27;Who may apply&#x27; sheet).</li><li lang=\"en\">If you asked for a mail ballot but want to vote in person, bring it to an early voting site or your polling place to be voided; if you never got it, sign a statement saying so.</li><li lang=\"en\">The State Board&#x27;s documents differ in detail on one point: its FAQ gives October 29 as the request deadline without separating in-person delivery; its &#x27;Who may apply&#x27; sheet says an application delivered in person may be made up to one day before the election.</li></ul></div><details class=\"lmore\" data-lv=\"3\" data-open-lv=\"5\"><summary data-t=\"061i9ua\" data-tv=\"{&quot;0&quot;:&quot;4&quot;}\">Where this comes from: 4 pages of <span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span>&rsquo;s election office, its laws and the federal guide</summary><ol class=\"vbm-src\"><li><a href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmJ%2bGs6YFATVXPZF6r1FbitENUkm%2fywKrEQArnBU6aOPGahVJq1yE9PG9ksIX8KZJgTJ0G5ME8mTXm2phBu7K0HRGxGCxNtZaL%2b1iPXZ9SlCSPTm68r48uJcHoU8RSIsyrXM3nKvqxLmJAufgl412N%2fQ%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" lang=\"en\">2026 Vote-By-Mail Frequently Asked Questions (rev. 8/2026)</a>, <span lang=\"en\">Illinois State Board of Elections</span> <small data-t=\"0s8lmsi\">(official page; read <time datetime=\"2026-10-21\" data-tf=\"{&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;,&quot;year&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">October 21, 2026</time>)</small></li><li><a href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/NewDocDisplay.aspx?%2fM0cs48zOKUVo8NHFkkNhVwyxu6isYxmj2awazxG5oLYFkE33dlxTqFgJUGePoYJvFoQzCF0NPPhk%2bkCUeTnMY7WNUFQszxqTDQ9jXur%2fsETCB7SX822PFAg5OWTXYGBk9j5PCx45ROsQc0E6Cb0pA%3d%3d\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" lang=\"en\">Voting by Mail: Who May Apply for a Vote By Mail Ballot? (10 ILCS 5/19, 5/20)</a>, <span lang=\"en\">Illinois State Board of Elections</span> <small data-t=\"0s8lmsi\">(official page; read <time datetime=\"2026-10-21\" data-tf=\"{&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;,&quot;year&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">October 21, 2026</time>)</small></li><li><a href=\"https://www.elections.il.gov/ElectionOperations/VotingByMail.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" lang=\"en\">Voting by Mail: Next Election, 2026 General Election</a>, <span lang=\"en\">Illinois State Board of Elections</span> <small data-t=\"0s8lmsi\">(official page; read <time datetime=\"2026-10-21\" data-tf=\"{&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;,&quot;year&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">October 21, 2026</time>)</small></li><li><a href=\"https://move.elections.il.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" lang=\"en\">Illinois Military and Overseas Voter Empowerment (MOVE)</a>, <span lang=\"en\">Illinois State Board of Elections</span> <small data-t=\"0s8lmsi\">(official page; read <time datetime=\"2026-10-21\" data-tf=\"{&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;,&quot;year&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">October 21, 2026</time>)</small></li></ol></details><p class=\"vbm-ck\" data-t=\"0u78ne0\">Checked <time datetime=\"2026-10-21\" data-tf=\"{&quot;month&quot;:&quot;long&quot;,&quot;day&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;,&quot;year&quot;:&quot;numeric&quot;}\">October 21, 2026</time>. Rules and dates can change: <span data-t=\"0zjq1mk\">Illinois</span>&rsquo;s election office, and your county or local election office, have the final word. <a href=\"../faq/\">More questions about voting</a>.</p><p class=\"holder\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tca-share\" data-share data-share-url=\"https://thecivicarchive.org/ballot/il/#mail\" data-share-title=\"Vote by mail or absentee in Illinois\" data-share-text=\"Vote by mail or absentee in Illinois: the deadlines, how to ask for a ballot and how to send it back, from the state&#x27;s own pages (checked October 21, 2026). The Civic Archive\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"5\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"19\" r=\"3\"/><path d=\"M8.6 13.5l6.8 4M15.4 6.5l-6.8 4\"/></svg><span data-t=\"0m2bcgo\">Share</span></button></p></section>"}